&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;About Wolt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we’re building the delivery of (almost) everything and you’ll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Wolt isn’t always easy, but it’s definitely exciting. Here you’ll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You’ll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you’re a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced Platform Engineer to join Event Streaming team — the distributed team responsible for the Kafka infrastructure and event streaming systems that power business-critical workflows across Wolt, Deliveroo and DoorDash.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining a team that operates at the intersection of Platform Engineering and Reliability Engineering, building and running the streaming backbone that is used by thousands of services across 3 companies. This is deeply technical work: you&#39;ll own distributed systems at scale, contribute to long-term architecture decisions, and be working on the reliability of critical parts of infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be joining the team within the broader Storage organisation. The team builds and operates highly reliable, scalable and efficient event streaming infrastructure, including Kafka, in-house Event Streaming abstraction (internally called Event Bus) and any future streaming platform technologies. These systems support critical workflows and are foundational to how engineering teams build reliable, event-driven products at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here’s what your day-to-day might look like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build and operate large-scale, event streaming infrastructure that supports critical production workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability, scalability, observability and automation of Kafka, Event Bus and related streaming components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug complex distributed systems issues — latency issues, performance bottlenecks, capacity constraints, partition imbalances — and drive them to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build infrastructure automation and self-healing capabilities that reduce operational toil and improve platform resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the team’s 24/7 On-call rotation and incident response, and drive continuous improvement through pre-mortems, operational readiness checklists and post-mortem action items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with other teams within Storage organization and wider Core Infrastructure org, like SRE, Data Platform, and Caching teams across EU and US regions — including occasional collaboration in the EU evening hours.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the long-term architecture and evolution of our event streaming platform, contributing to RFCs and technical strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Need to Thrive&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience building or operating distributed systems in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with Kafka or similar event streaming systems, either as a platform, infrastructure service or critical production dependency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding ability in Java, Go, Python or similar — with the emphasis on building reliable, production-grade systems and libraries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating scalable production infrastructure, including debugging, troubleshooting and improving reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of infrastructure automation, observability, capacity management and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good fundamentals in Linux, networking and JVM-based systems, or curiosity to deepen expertise in these areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and writing skills, with the ability to work across platform, infrastructure and product engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to Kafka or related open source distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Redpanda, WarpStream, AutoMQ, Pulsar or similar streaming technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with JVM tuning, broker tuning, partition management or Cruise Control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with tiered storage, diskless streaming architectures or multi-region event streaming platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ncz4s_oBczc&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;About Wolt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we’re building the delivery of (almost) everything and you’ll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Wolt isn’t always easy, but it’s definitely exciting. Here you’ll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You’ll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you’re a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Wolt, we create technology that brings local communities, merchants and customers closer together. What started with restaurant delivery has grown into a broader local commerce platform, helping customers discover and access more of what their cities have to offer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Retail business continues to grow, we’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Sales Regional Enterprise Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to expand our selection of high-value regional retail partners. You’ll join our Enterprise Sales team and take ownership of some of the most important regional acquisition opportunities across priority retail verticals, helping shape what customers can find on Wolt in their cities. &lt;strong&gt;This role can be based in Berlin, Cologne or Frankfurt.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll own the acquisition and development of high-value regional Enterprise retail partners in Germany, from identifying and engaging the right prospects through commercial negotiations, signing and initial rollout. You’ll combine strong commercial execution with a strategic view on which partners can have the greatest impact on Wolt’s selection, coverage and long-term growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day-to-day in this role you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end sales cycle for regional Enterprise retail opportunities, from prospecting and qualification through negotiation, contracting and signing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a high-quality pipeline of larger regional retailers and multi-location partners across priority verticals such as grocery, convenience, pet, pharmacy and beauty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of prospective partners’ businesses and create compelling commercial propositions that demonstrate the value of partnering with Wolt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex commercial negotiations, balancing partner needs with sustainable economics and Wolt’s long-term business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with senior decision-makers and act as a trusted commercial partner throughout the sales process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with internal teams including Operations, Account Management, Finance, Legal, Marketing and Product to structure partnerships and enable successful launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership beyond the signature, ensuring a strong handover and initial rollout so that newly acquired partners can successfully go live and scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use market insights, pipeline data and commercial learnings to identify opportunities, prioritize the highest-impact accounts and continuously improve our regional Enterprise sales approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to sharing best practices and raising the bar for Enterprise sales execution across the wider team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our humble expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have significant experience in B2B sales, business development or strategic partnerships, ideally working with Enterprise or other complex, multi-stakeholder customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong track record of independently managing and closing complex commercial opportunities from initial outreach through contract signature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an excellent negotiator and understand how to build partnerships that create sustainable value for both sides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable engaging and influencing senior stakeholders, both externally and across cross-functional internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You combine a hands-on, results-oriented sales mindset with strong commercial judgment and the ability to prioritize opportunities based on their strategic impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re highly structured and comfortable managing multiple opportunities and stakeholders simultaneously while maintaining strong attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable working with data and commercial metrics to evaluate opportunities, build business cases and inform decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly and persuasively and are fluent in English and German.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to play a meaningful role in the next phase of Wolt’s Retail growth. You’ll have direct ownership of high-impact regional partnerships and the autonomy to take opportunities from first conversation all the way through to launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work at the intersection of sales, strategy and operations, collaborating with experienced colleagues across Wolt while building relationships with some of the most important retailers in the market. The role offers substantial commercial ownership and exposure while giving you the opportunity to develop further in Enterprise sales and contribute to how we scale our Retail business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also join a fast-moving international environment where good ideas can quickly turn into action, with the tools, support and trust to take ownership of your work and make a visible impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like an opportunity you’d be excited about, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After you apply, our Talent Acquisition team will review your application and get in touch with selected candidates for an initial conversation. The process will typically include interviews with the hiring team and relevant stakeholders, giving you the opportunity to learn more about the role, team and business while we get to know your experience and approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the role and location, the process may also include a practical case or commercial exercise. We’ll share the exact interview steps and expectations with you as you progress through the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/GoL541_xj9w&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;About Wolt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we’re building the delivery of (almost) everything and you’ll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Wolt isn’t always easy, but it’s definitely exciting. Here you’ll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You’ll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you’re a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Data Developer Experience team is looking for a &lt;span class=&quot;job-application__name&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;job-application-title&quot;&gt;Senior Software Engineer &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;to build core services for our Data Platform. The team builds the Data Control Plane, a Go-based internal Terraform- or Kubernetes-like platform which allows users and other services to configure and operate Data Platform infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to meet the massive data scaling needs of a global organization with a platform that is simple yet powerful, self-healing, agentic-safe, trustworthy, snappy, and cost efficient.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Designing&lt;/strong&gt; - you align our ambitions and stakeholder needs on a feature level. You collaborate with the team to propose well fitting solutions using RFCs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building&lt;/strong&gt; - you develop Go code with agents. The implementation may target a backend service, our plugin framework, CLI tooling, CI/CD pipelines, or even our React frontend app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documenting&lt;/strong&gt; - you ensure high quality, curated markdown documentation for users, AI agents, and maintainers / on-call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operating&lt;/strong&gt; - you strive for operational excellence with constant vigilance, proactivity, and on-call participation to ensure we provide a robust platform for business critical workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supporting&lt;/strong&gt; - you understand the needs of diverse data platform users and guide them to golden paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our humble expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a proven track record of designing, building, and operating large-scale distributed systems and/or platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring deep experience with Go, but you possess a polyglot mindset and are happy to dive into Python or other languages when the problem calls for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have hands-on experience building, maintaining, and optimizing CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You possess a strong foundational understanding of networking and security best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are familiar with data platform architecture and technologies, specifically columnar databases/storage and MPP engines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are passionate about Developer Experience and excel at balancing user needs with technical and platform constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You actively leverage agentic coding as your preferred workflow to accelerate value delivery, while maintaining the critical eye needed to rigorously vet and secure code for robust systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A rare opportunity to join a near-greenfield project building state-of-the-art, robust, scalable foundations for the future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a Big Tech-adjacent environment with brilliant colleagues, modern tooling and practices, and large scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
